# Copy to .env and fill in. Nothing here is read by the app any more except
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL and EXPO_PUBLIC_API_SECRET — since TODOS A3 every
# provider key lives on the server, and the app talks only to the server.

# ─── Provider keys (SERVER ONLY) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# In production these are `fly secrets set` under their PLAIN names
# (OPENAI_API_KEY, not EXPO_PUBLIC_OPENAI_API_KEY). server/index.ts prefers the
# plain name and falls back to the EXPO_PUBLIC_ one for local dev, because
# dashboard/server.ts and scripts/scrape-nurseries.ts still read the prefixed
# names directly. Unifying that is TODOS H1.

# PlantNet — species identification. https://my.plantnet.org
EXPO_PUBLIC_PLANTNET_API_KEY=your_plantnet_api_key_here
# OpenAI — GPT-5.5 vision health assessment + scraper extraction/verification.
# https://platform.openai.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here
# Firecrawl — primary nursery page scraper. https://firecrawl.dev
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=your_firecrawl_api_key_here
# Tavily Extract — fallback when Firecrawl fails or returns empty. Optional;
# omit to disable the fallback (the scraper still works). https://tavily.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_TAVILY_API_KEY=your_tavily_api_key_here
# Google Places API (New) — nursery discovery, and the in-app map.
# Requesting websiteUri bills the Enterprise SKU. Restrict the key to the app
# bundle ID in the Cloud console (TODOS P0) or it is free quota for whoever
# extracts it from the bundle.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=your_google_maps_api_key_here
# Plant.id v3 — disease classification. Present but unused until TODOS E1.
EXPO_PUBLIC_PLANTID_API_KEY=your_plantid_api_key_here

# ─── Backend (READ BY THE APP) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the app sends photos and nursery searches. Locally this is your Mac's
# LAN IP so the simulator and a real device both reach it — re-check it with
# `ipconfig getifaddr en0`, it changes whenever DHCP moves the machine. In
# production it is the deployed URL (https://plantai-api.fly.dev).
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:4000

# ─── Gate (READ BY BOTH) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app sends EXPO_PUBLIC_API_SECRET as the `x-plantai-key` header; the server
# compares it to API_SHARED_SECRET. Same value, two names — the split exists so
# the server half can be a `fly secret` while the app half is a build constant.
#
# ⚠️ NOT AUTHENTICATION. It ships inside the app bundle by necessity, and anyone
# holding a build can extract it in about a minute. It raises the cost of casual
# abuse. DAILY_REQUEST_CAP is the thing that actually bounds the bill. See
# server/gate.ts before building anything that assumes this endpoint is secure.
#
# Generate one: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
API_SHARED_SECRET=generate_one_and_use_the_same_value_below
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_SECRET=generate_one_and_use_the_same_value_above

# ─── Gate tuning (SERVER ONLY, all optional) ──────────────────────────────────
# log     = allow everything, log what enforcing would have blocked (default)
# enforce = actually block
# Stay on log until an `eas update` carrying the secret reaches installed apps
# (TODOS A4). Enforcing first locks every existing build, including yours, out.
GATE_MODE=log
# Hard ceiling on billable requests per UTC day. This is the real spend guard:
# each nursery search costs 1 Places search + N Firecrawl scrapes + N OpenAI
# passes; each diagnosis costs 1 PlantNet + 1 OpenAI vision call.
DAILY_REQUEST_CAP=200
# Per-IP burst limit. Job polling is exempt — an eight-minute scrape polled
# every few seconds would otherwise rate-limit the client out of its own result.
RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN=6
# Emit CORS headers for this origin only. Unset = no CORS header at all, which
# is correct for the native app. Set it only if a browser needs to call the API.
# CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
